; Manifest-phase family, 3 of 6, and the first error-severity one.
;
; `:sjon` declares which manifest format version the plugin is written
; against. The host implements `Plugin.SUPPORTED_SJON_FORMAT`; `9.9` is
; newer, so the host cannot know what the manifest means and refuses it
; rather than reading it as best it can. This is the forward-compatibility
; escape hatch that lets the format grow — a v9.9 manifest reaching a v1.1
; host must fail loudly, not partially load.
;
; The trailing `unknown_form` is the consequence: an error-severity manifest
; diagnostic drops the plugin from the schema, so `pt` is no longer
; declared by anything. Compare `manifest-license-unrecognized`, which warns
; and keeps the plugin.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0" :sjon "9.9"
  (form :name pt (key :name x :type number)))

(pt :x 1)
